{
  "name": "skink",
  "_about": "SCULPTED (2026-11-21, tools/creaturegen/rework/herps/skink.py): the FIVE-LINED SKINK, Plestiodon fasciatus, 18 cm, the tail 60% of it. A smooth CYLINDRICAL body low to the ground with no waist -- the neck as thick as the head, the tail as thick again at its root, tapering long; a conical head with a flat crown and a blunt-pointed snout, small eyes with lids, the ear opening behind the jaw; SHORT legs, small five-toed clawed feet; SMOOTH GLOSSY overlapping scales (`rowscales`, wet). FIVE PALE STRIPES on dark brown (paints): down the spine, high on each side, and low on each flank through the ear, running onto the tail. Coats: adult (brown, cream stripes), juvenile (black, bright stripes, a BLUE TAIL), old male (the stripes faded, the head and jaws orange). A quick sinuous scurry, the tail swinging.",
